# Line endings, because this repository publishes files people hash.
#
# `editions/` carries artifacts whose sha256 is committed in the manifest
# beside them, and `editions/README.md` tells a reader to check one against
# the other. Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would check
# those files out as CRLF and make every digest disagree with the file it
# describes -- a buyer following the instructions would conclude they had been
# handed tampered bytes. The files are committed as they were rendered, LF;
# this keeps the distribution channel from rewriting them.
editions/** -text
